The live page sells 0-10 V dimming, which the design has not had since V10. Tell him today, with the coordinator's pick to drop it, and change the line once he says OK.

The pick is sound. Keeping 0-10 V needs no new part, since the ERP driver already does 0-10 V. It needs:
- a second, separate low-voltage way in, through the plate on the Class 2 side of the tray;
- a ceiling-box arrangement that keeps the control pair apart from the 120 V splices;
- a redraw of the canopy's inside;
- an extra pair of wires to a 0-10 V control on every install that uses it.

Only venues whose lights run on a 0-10 V control system lose out, and a phase-cut dimmer on that circuit works for them. Nobody has bought one ('Nothing is built yet'), so no harm has been done yet.

